from pathlib import Path
import sys,json,hashlib,shutil,re
from html.parser import HTMLParser
cap=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;root=Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve();dist=root/'dist';dest=dist/'sources/monitor-admission-v0.1';dest.mkdir(exist_ok=False);home=hashlib.sha256((dist/'index.html').read_bytes()).hexdigest()
for name in ['REPORT.md','CONTRACT.json','CONFIG.json','admit_monitor.py','build_and_test.py','SYNTHETIC_PACKET.json','SYNTHETIC_CATALOG.json','ACQUISITION_PROFILE_FIXTURE.json','TAIL_BOUND_PROPOSAL_FIXTURE.json','TEST_RESULTS.json','CIRCUIT_DISPOSITION.json']:shutil.copyfile(cap/name,dest/name)
main='''<main id="main"><div class="atlas-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Overview</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/evidence/">Evidence</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Monitor receipt graph</span></div><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">23 October 2026 Chicago · Monitor admission contract 0.1</div><h1>Nine evidence roles.<br>One unsigned tail proposal.</h1><p class="lede">A versioned receipt graph binds sampled-monitor data, clock calibration, I/Q errors, source preparation and independent outside-model evidence to the conditional leakage calculation.</p></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Constructor software checks · Synthetic fixtures · Physical Promotion 0</strong><p>57 controls pass: one author-controlled positive fixture and 56 rejection cases. Independent review remains pending. No calibration truth, reviewer identity or physical independence is inferred. The historical circuit candidate and EXIT-03 remain HOLD.</p></aside><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/monitor-admission-v0.1/REPORT.md">Read scope and review requirements ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/monitor-admission-v0.1/CONTRACT.json">Machine-readable contract</a></div><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>The measurement prerequisites are explicit.</h2><table><tbody><tr><th>Data and timing</th><td>Exact sample bytes, ordered indices, timestamp bytes and reviewed metrology</td></tr><tr><th>Measurement path</th><td>Full I/Q path and residual extraction; charged 10/5/3/2 µV error shares</td></tr><tr><th>Independent source evidence</th><td>Fixed finite-mode preparation and outside-model spectral variation ≤10 µV</td></tr><tr><th>Transfer and computation</th><td>Same preparation, residual reference, run and epoch; pinned source hashes and exact arithmetic</td></tr></tbody></table><p>All roles bind the acquisition profile, channels, epoch, units, kernel and source-contract hash. Every receipt binds the evidence and witness bytes. A separate review process must control the trusted configuration and receipt allowlist.</p><p>Submitted timestamps alone are not calibration. A later monitor on the same device cannot certify a historical waveform without the required reviewed transfer.</p></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Structural readiness stops before scientific acceptance.</h2><p>The frozen design still gives the conditional tail ceiling 3627/4000000 V = 0.90675 mV. The checker replays exact digital energy/RMS and the rational sampled-Gram certificate.</p><p>Its output is an unsigned tail-bound proposal, not a v0.1 acquisition evidence packet or an approved receipt. The original twelve-role checker is unchanged. The other eleven acquisition requirements remain necessary, and no action-scale estimate follows.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/monitor-admission-v0.1/TAIL_BOUND_PROPOSAL_FIXTURE.json">Unsigned synthetic proposal ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/sampled-monitor/">Prior conditional theorem →</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Tests reach the intended rejection gates.</h2><p>Controls cover run/channel/source mismatch, stale calibration, timestamp deviations, I/Q undercharging, unsupported outside-model evidence, alias intrusion, source-code changes and transitive cycles. Semantic mutations rebind synthetic receipt hashes so a hash error does not hide the tested gate.</p><p>A changed low-RMS sample still invalidates a stale computation certificate. The synthetic reviewer labels are author controlled and confer no independent authority.</p><p>The unchanged historical checker still returns HOLD. No empirical monitor dataset or reviewed calibration has been supplied in the scoped record.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/monitor-admission-v0.1/TEST_RESULTS.json">All 57 software controls ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/monitor-admission-v0.1/admit_monitor.py">Checker source ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/monitor-admission-v0.1/SYNTHETIC_PACKET.json">Synthetic packet ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/evidence-admission/">Acquisition evidence contract →</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Next: independent witness methods.</h2><p>Specify source completeness, the independent 10 µV outside-model TV witness and full-path calibration for review before measurement. These must address unknown aliases and the same residual transfer across both observation intervals. Physical Promotion remains 0.</p></div></section></main>'''
template=(dist/'evidence/sampled-monitor/index.html').read_text();page=re.sub(r'<title>.*?</title>','<title>Sampled-monitor receipt graph · Unified Dynamics</title>',template,count=1);page=re.sub(r'<main\b[\s\S]*?</main>',lambda _:main,page,count=1);folder=dist/'evidence/monitor-admission';folder.mkdir(exist_ok=False);(folder/'index.html').write_text(page);(cap/'PUBLIC_PAGE.html').write_text(page)
card='''<article class="claim" id="monitor-admission-v01"><div class="eyebrow">23 October 2026 Chicago · Monitor receipt graph 0.1</div><h2>Nine roles bind the sampled-monitor evidence</h2><p>57 constructor software controls verify bindings, exact arithmetic and rejection gates. The unsigned tail proposal requires independent review; the historical candidate remains HOLD. Physical Promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/monitor-admission/">Read receipt contract and limits →</a></article>'''
